WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Good morning, John.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.920
So, a couple months ago, you were like...

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:06.060
[John]: "I think the underlying problem is that almost everything on the internet is dependent upon advertising,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.020
and advertisers, in my opinion, are terrible at measuring the value in the creator-viewer relationship.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.080
So, Hank, please fix this problem during my paternity leave, okay? Thanks."

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.500
And then, you had a baby, seen here in this professional artist's rendering,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.560
and I set off, on my own, to solve this extraordinarily complicated problem.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.140
And, not to brag, but I think that I have done it, so without further ado,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.880
I must announce that John and I will be stopping the vlogbrothers channel and instead,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.700
be doing a series of nerdy workout videos called Super Cardio Brothers!

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.780
Okay, despite the fact that this is an amazing idea, it does not actually solve the problem.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.400
The problem we are solving as someone on Twitter so succinctly put it is that

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.060
"advertisers value views, not viewers."

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.940
They don't care how much you care about the thing you're watching, they only care that you're watching.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:55.140
This - it turns out - is not a problem that I can solve, but it might be a problem that we can solve.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.260
The advertising system is so ingrained that there isn't a technological solution,

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.200
but there might be a cultural solution.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.400
Cultural changes need activation energy and they need catalysts.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.320
Nerdfighteria has become kind of a pretty powerful force.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.200
So I feel like Nerdfighteria can be the activation energy and Subbable could be the catalyst.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.380
Subbable, if you haven't already heard of it, is a system that lets you subscribe to content

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.260
and when you do that, you get to decide how much you would like to pay for it.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.020
It could be $0 a month or it could be $1 a month or $5 a month or $100 a month.

00:01:23.026 --> 00:01:26.366
Or it could just be a one-time amount of money, we're pretty flexible.

00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:31.480
Subscribers get videos and other content in their feed and possibly maybe some other exclusive content.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.600
But you don't have to pay for it.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.720
Every dollar you do spend, gets banked in the Subbable system,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.280
and you can trade that in for perks for that project.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.560
That might be a signed poster, or a mention in a episode,

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.220
or a message to your loved one in the description.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.900
We're launching this with just Crash Course, Crash Course is our educational show,

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.100
it is very expensive to make.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.520
The Google grant that payed for it for the last 2 years is ending,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.760
and without this system and without the support of the people who like it,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.020
we won't be able to keep doing it.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:02.200
Because it's actually educational content and thus incapable of getting the bajillion views

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.640
necessary to pay for it through advertising.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.760
Crash Course will of course still live on Youtube,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.780
it will still be free, but our hope is that enough people who can pay for it,

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.200
and we understand that lots of people can't, will choose to so that all people can have access to it.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.760
We're asking, and this is weird,

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.460
for you to pay for content because you want to, not because you're forced to.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.180
This is a weird cultural shift.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.060
We want to continue educating the world for free,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.760
as effectively as possible and that takes money.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.040
We also want you to help us create that cultural change,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:36.260
a change that I think will result in a lot more content being created that's really engaging,

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.720
that people really love and isn't just distracting.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.500
We wouldn't have been able to do this without Peter Jaros, our developer

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.240
or Andrew Willis, our designer.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.040
They are both, really fantastic.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.740
And also, of course we wouldn't be able to do it without the support of Nerdfighteria.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:48.880
Thanks, guys.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.000
John, its been wonderful to share this channel with so many amazing people over the last few weeks,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.640
during your paternity leave. But I am somewhat relieved, and very excited to say,

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.380
that I will see you. On Tuesday.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.440
Subbable, it's a little hard to spell.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.720
S-U-B-B-A-B-L-E.com

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:08.160
Go there, help us fund Crash Course and defy capitalism.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.100
Brwrwrwrwrwrwrwr!

